Armenian soprano Anna Avdalyan has been a permanent ensemble member of the Schleswig-Holstein State Theatre since January 2023.

At the Schleswig-Holstein State Theatre, she has developed a versatile repertoire spanning opera, operetta and musical theatre. Her roles there include Constance in Poulenc’s *Dialogues des Carmélites*, Mabel in Gilbert and Sullivan’s *The Pirates of Penzance*, Susanna in Mozart’s *Le nozze di Figaro*, as well as Molly in *One Touch of Venus* and Lisa in *Jekyll & Hyde*.

Prior to joining the ensemble in Flensburg, she held a permanent engagement at the Theatre Görlitz-Zittau, where she performed, among other roles, Anna in *Der liebe Augustin* and Papagena and the Queen of the Night in Mozart’s *Die Zauberflöte*.

While still completing her studies, Anna Avdalyan gained her first professional stage experience at several German theatres. Her early engagements included the Schleswig-Holstein State Theatre, the Theatre Görlitz-Zittau and the Bavarian State Opera in Munich, where she appeared as an Ursuline in Krzysztof Penderecki’s *The Devils of Loudun*.

She studied voice at the University of Music and Performing Arts Stuttgart with Professor Ulrike Sonntag. After graduating with distinction with a Bachelor’s degree in 2019, she continued her studies in the Master’s programme in Opera, which she successfully completed in 2022. In recognition of her artistic achievements, she received second prize at the Lions Club Competition in Stuttgart as well as the Trude Eipperle-Rieger Prize. Alongside her studies, she pursued an active concert career, performing as a soloist in oratorios, concert works and recitals. She also gained extensive experience in contemporary music. Her repertoire encompasses works from a wide range of periods and styles, including compositions by Mozart, Bach and Orff.

Anna Avdalyan began her musical education in Armenia, where she studied musicology at the Komitas State Conservatory in Yerevan. At the same time, she performed as a soloist with the professional State Chamber Choir of Armenia under the direction of Robert Mlqeyan, becoming a permanent member of the choir at the age of 18. During this period, she gained extensive concert and performance experience. In 2015, she appeared as a soloist with the Our Lady of Armenia Choir at St. Peter’s Basilica in Rome, performing before Pope Francis. Her musical journey had begun much earlier: as a child, she already gained stage experience through concert tours and regular performances, developing a deep connection with music and singing.

As a coloratura soprano, Anna Avdalyan particularly enjoys exploring the virtuosity of the operatic coloratura repertoire alongside the diverse sound worlds of different musical genres. She is equally passionate about the combination of singing and acting and about exploring new forms of musical expression.
